# DISABLED EXAMPLE. Rename to 50-saml-config.caddy inside the gateway's
# /etc/caddy/routes.d/ to serve the SAML configuration routes; move it to off/
# and `caddy reload` to take them away.
#
# SAML 2.0 single sign-on, configuration side (backend-rs/src/routes/saml.rs):
#   GET, PUT, DELETE /api/v1/auth/saml/config
#   GET              /api/v1/auth/saml/sp-metadata
#
# NEW ROUTES, RUST ONLY: unlike every other file in this directory there is no
# Python implementation of these paths, so this group has NO FAILOVER and no
# kill switch back to Python. The upstream list names `api-rs` alone: with it
# down (or this file moved to off/) the admin card answers 502/404 and nothing
# else changes. People can still sign in through SAML in that case, because
# the sign-in endpoints are Python and read the rows Rust already wrote.
#
# NOT in this file, and they must stay on Python (no matcher below touches
# them): GET /api/v1/auth/saml/start and POST /api/v1/auth/saml/acs. They end
# in session issuance and run the assertion validation
# (backend/auth/saml/). The path matcher is exact so a future route under
# /auth/saml/ does not silently move here.
#
# Needs: ENTERPRISE_SSO_ENABLED on both services (the routes answer 409
# `sso_instance_disabled` otherwise) and the same DATABASE_URL.

@rs_saml_config {
	method GET PUT DELETE
	path /api/v1/auth/saml/config /api/v1/auth/saml/sp-metadata
}
handle @rs_saml_config {
	reverse_proxy api-rs:8021 {
		health_uri /health
		health_interval 5s
		health_timeout 2s
	}
}
